{
  "name": "Ensnaring Strike",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>As you hit the target, grasping vines appear on it, and it makes a Strength saving throw. A Large or larger creature has Advantage on this save. On a failed save, the target has the <span style=\"font-family:Signika, sans-serif\">&amp;Reference[restrained apply=false] </span>condition until the spell ends. On a successful save, the vines shrivel away, and the spell ends.</p><p>While Restrained, the target takes 1d6 Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. The target or a creature within reach of it can take an action to make a [[/check ability=str skill=ath dc=@attributes.spell.dc]] check against your spell save DC. On a success, the spell ends.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1.</p><div class=\"cat-description\"><p><em>midi-qol: Cast it at the creature you just hit. Large or larger creatures have advantage on the save. While Ensnared the target takes the piercing damage at the start of each of its turns, and can use its action for an Athletics check against your spell save DC to escape (a chat card at the start of its turn). A creature freeing it is not automated.</em></p><p><em>Automation requires Coven's Automation Toolkit (CAT).</em></p></div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
